            </table>
          </div>
          <p>
            <strong>What the model leaves out.</strong> Finding, tracking and holding the beam on
            the target; time spent moving between targets; eclipse and operational downtime; and
            the propellant the craft spends keeping station as its target descends. Each one makes
            the real times longer. The model also assumes the pulse arrives at a fluence that
            couples well, which for a 5 J pulse means a spot about a centimetre across.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
